{"pageid":2621,"title":"Fruits","displaytitle":"<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Fruits</span>","revid":22155,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Spawning\">Spawning</span></h2>\n<p>Fruits spawn on various trees and bushes in Oaklands depended on type of tree, tree and bush location and biome. Fruits can be harvested by grabbing them from the tree or chopping the tree down. Some fruit will die (disappear not long after you cut the tree) if you chop down the tree (unless you are using the <a href=\"/wiki/Living_Axe\" title=\"Living Axe\">Living Axe</a>), it's better to harvest by hand if you want to get more quantity (if you do not have the Living Axe). Fruits spawn on the leaves of trees or near the top of the tree on the bark.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Uses\">Uses</span></h2>\n<p>Fruit can be sold raw but will net a lower profit. It can also be turned into jam by using the <a href=\"/wiki/Press_Machine\" title=\"Press Machine\">Press Machine</a> to convert the fruit to its respective Jam, by including the fruit as well as an empty <a href=\"/wiki/Jar\" title=\"Jar\">jar</a>. The Jam can be sold for profit; each type of jam will sell for 4x the base price of the fruit used. Note: Jams give back the empty jar when sold. Additionally, eating fruits gives temporary effects to the player. Consuming jam gives the same effect for significantly more time. (More research needed for effect durations)\n</p>\n<table class=\"fandom-table article-table sortable\">\n<caption>Fruits\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th class=\"unsortable\">Fruit Names\n</th>\n<th class=\"unsortable\">Fruit Images\n</th>\n<th data-sort-type=\"currency\">Fruit Value\n</th>\n<th>Jam Value\n</th>\n<th class=\"unsortable\">Jam Names\n</th>\n<th class=\"unsortable\">Jam Images\n</th>\n<th class=\"unsortable\">Where to Find:\n</th>\n<th>Approximate money earning speed (not counting travel time)\n</th>\n<th>Consum